1. ls | grep txt

ls lists all files.
Output is sent through pipe | to grep.
grep txt shows only filenames containing "txt".

xv6 has ls, but it does not have the grep command by default.

2.echo "hello world" | wc -w

echo prints the text.
Pipe sends the text to wc.
wc -w counts the number of words.

output in linux :
2

xv6 does not have the wc command with the -w option.
xv6 has only a small set of user programs.

3.cat file.txt | head -5

cat file.txt displays the file contents.
Pipe sends output to head.
head -5 displays only the first 5 lines.

xv6 has cat, but it does not include the head command.
